== Geography ==

Krishna district is surrounded on the east by [[Bay of Bengal]], west by [[Guntur district|Guntur]] and [[Bapatla district|Bapatla]] districts and north by [[Eluru district|Eluru]] and [[NTR district|NTR]] districts and south by [[Bay of Bengal]]. It occupies an area of {{convert|3775|km2|sqmi}}.{{Sfn|CPO|2022|p=VII}} It has a total coastline of {{cvt|88|km}}.{{Sfn|CPO|2022|p=1}}

=== Flora and fauna ===

The forest occupies only 9 percent of the total undivided district area. However, it contains reserved forest areas in [[Nandigama]], [[Vijayawada]], [[Tiruvuru]], [[Nuzvid]], [[Gannavaram]], [[Machilipatnam]] and Divi Seema Talukas. A type of light wood known as ‘Ponuku’ (Gyrocapus Jacquini) is found in the Kondapalli hills. The wood is used for the manufacture of the well known [[Kondapalli Toys|Kondpalli]] toys. The most noticeable trees are pterocarpus, Terminalia, Anogeissus and Logustroeinai and Casuarina.<ref name="flora and fauna">{{cite web |title=Flora and Fauna of Krishna district |url=http://forest.ap.nic.in/WL%20KRISHNA.htm |publisher=AP forest department |access-date=14 July 2014 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140125021525/http://forest.ap.nic.in/WL%20KRISHNA.htm |archive-date=25 January 2014}}</ref>

Panthers, dholes, jungle cats, foxes, bears and other carnivorous mammalian fauna are found here. Deer, spotted deer, sambar, blackbuck and other herbivorous animals are found in the inland forests. The district has a large number of Murrah buffaloes and cows.<ref name="flora and fauna" />

=== Climate ===

The climatic conditions of the district consist of extremely hot summers and moderately hot winters and may be classified as tropical. The period starting from April to June is the hottest. The annual rainfall in the region is about 1047.68&nbsp;mm and 66% of it is contributed to by the Southwest monsoon.{{Sfn|CPO|2022|p=II}}

Black Cotton (57.6 percent), Sand clay loams (22.3 percent), Red loams (19.4 percent), and sandy soils account for balance 0.7% in the district.{{Sfn|CPO|2022|p=II}}

