== Economy ==

Agriculture is the main stay of economy. [[Paddy (unmilled rice)|Paddy]] is the main food crop cultivated. Based on 2019–20 data, the gross cropped area of the district was 3.76 lakh hectares of which gross irrigated area was 2.42 lakh hectares.{{Sfn|CPO|2022|p=III}} Other products produced include [[sugarcane]], [[mango]], tomato, milk, meat and [[Fishery|fisheries]].

== Transport ==

=== Road ===
[[National Highway 65 (India)|NH 65]] from [[Pune]] to [[Machilipatnam]], [[National Highway 165 (India)|NH 165]] from [[Pamarru, Krishna district|Pamarru]] to [[Palakollu]], [[National Highway 216 (India)|NH 216]] from [[Ongole]] to [[Kattipudi|Kathipudi]] pass through the district.

=== Rail ===
There exists {{cvt|97|km}} of rail network in the district. [[Gudivada Junction railway station]] and [[Machilipatnam railway station]] are prominent railway stations in the district. Nearest major railway station is [[Vijayawada Junction railway station]] at a distance of 80Km from Machilipatnam by train.<ref name="howtoreach"/>

=== Water ===
The [[Machilipatnam Port]] is currently under construction.<ref>{{Cite web |date=22 May 2023 |title=Andhra CM Jagan Reddy launches construction work of Rs 5,156 crore Machilipatnam port |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/cities/hyderabad/andhra-cm-jagan-reddy-launches-construction-work-machilipatnam-port-8622904/ |access-date=26 August 2023 |website=The Indian Express |language=en |archive-date=19 June 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240619054927/https://indianexpress.com/article/cities/hyderabad/andhra-cm-jagan-reddy-launches-construction-work-machilipatnam-port-8622904/ |url-status=live }}</ref>
The port will have an initial cargo capacity of 35 million tonnes (35 MMTPA), through four berths-three general cargo berths and one coal terminal. The port is scheduled to be completed in two years. In the future, the capacity of the four-berth deep water port will be increased to 116 million tonnes (116 MMTPA) as the cargo traffic increases gradually.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://news.abplive.com/news/andhra-pradesh-cm-jagan-reddy-launches-construction-work-of-rs-5-156-crore-machilipatnam-port-1604024 |title=Andhra CM Jagan Reddy Launches Construction Work of Rs 5,156 Crore Machilipatnam Port |date=22 May 2023 |access-date=26 April 2024 |archive-date=30 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231130095243/https://news.abplive.com/news/andhra-pradesh-cm-jagan-reddy-launches-construction-work-of-rs-5-156-crore-machilipatnam-port-1604024 |url-status=live }}</ref>

=== Air ===
Krishna district is served by [[Vijayawada Airport|Vijayawada International airport]] located in [[Gannavaram]] at a distance of 67.9&nbsp;km from Machilipatnam.<ref>{{Cite web |title=NTR Amaravati International Airport {{!}} Airports Authority of India |url=https://www.aai.aero/en/airports/vijayawada |access-date=5 April 2022 |archive-date=7 March 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220307202410/https://www.aai.aero/en/airports/vijayawada |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="howtoreach">{{Cite web |url=https://krishna.ap.gov.in/how-to-reach/ |title=How to reach |access-date=23 April 2023 |website=Krishna district |archive-date=23 April 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230423031838/https://krishna.ap.gov.in/how-to-reach/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

== Education ==

Dr.Gururaju Government Homoeo Medical college and Regional research institute for Homoeopathy are located in [[Gudivada]]. [[Krishna University]] is located in Machilipatnam.

== Culture ==

[[File:Kuchipudi Dancer Sahiti Ravali performing at Bhadrachalam 03.JPG|thumb|right|A [[Kuchipudi]] dancer performing on stage]]

The culture of Krishna district is mostly traditional in rural places and moderately modern in [[Gudivada]] and [[Machilipatnam]]. It is also famous as the birthplace for [[Indian classical dance]] named [[Kuchipudi]]. The dialect of Telugu spoken here is widely considered to be the standard form of Telugu.<ref>{{cite web |title=District profile |url=http://krishna.nic.in/ |website=Krishna District |publisher=National Informatics Centre |access-date=16 June 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140612095625/http://krishna.nic.in/ |archive-date=12 June 2014 |url-status=dead}}</ref>

== Sports ==

Chedugudu ([[Kabaddi]]) is the most popular sport, followed by [[cricket]], [[volleyball]], [[badminton]], [[basketball]] and [[tennis]]. [[N. T. Rama Rao|NTR]] Stadium is the main sports venue in [[Gudivada]]. It is used for several sports, like [[Sport of athletics|athletics]], [[volleyball]], [[cricket]] practice, [[kho kho]], [[kabaddi]], [[badminton]], [[tennis]] and [[basketball]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.thehindu.com/todays-paper/tp-national/tp-andhrapradesh/NTR-Stadium-all-set-to-become-more-sporty/article14772368.ece |title=NTR Stadium all set to become more sporty |work=The Hindu |date=2 June 2007 |url-status=live |url-access=subscription |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210406172529/https://www.thehindu.com/todays-paper/tp-national/tp-andhrapradesh/NTR-Stadium-all-set-to-become-more-sporty/article14772368.ece |archive-date=6 April 2021}}</ref> It is also the stadium for Krishna district cricket association.

==Tourism==
There are several places of tourist interest in the district. Some of them are given below.{{Sfn|CPO|2022|p=IV-V}}
[[File:Srikakulandhra Maha Vishnu Temple Panorama.jpg|right|thumb|Srikakulandhra Maha Vishnu Temple]]
* [[Kolleru Lake|Kolleru lake]] (Kaikaluru Mandal): largest freshwater lake
* [[Manginapudi Beach|Manginapudi]] beach: Natural beach
* [[Movva]]: Sri Movva Venugopala Swamy temple. Kshetrayya is said to have composed his famous lyrics here.
* [[Kuchipudi, Krishna district|Kuchipudi]]:the birth place of Siddhendra Yogi, the originator of the Kuchpudi dance
* [[Ghantasala, Krishna district|Ghantasala]]: once upon a time, a port and a halting place for Buddhist pilgrims and merchants travelling from Kalinga to Ceylone. Hindu and Buddhist Sculptures can be seen here
* [[Srikakulam, Krishna district|Srikakulam]] (Ghantasala Mandal): the historical capital of Andhra Empire of Goutamiputra Satakarni (AD 102–123). This is famous for the temple of Andhra Mahavishnu
* [[Hamsaladeevi]](Koduru Mandal): river Krishna drains into the Bay of Bengal at this place
* [[Gudivada]]: famous for Jain temple of Parswandha Swamy

== Notable people ==

* [[Kakarla Subba Rao]] was born in Pedamuttevi of Movva mandal and became the first director of Nizam's Institute of Medical Sciences, Hyderabad
* [[Tripuraneni Ramaswamy]] born in Angaluru of Gudlavalleru mandal was a poet and social reformer
* [[Kasinadhuni Nageswara Rao]] was born in Pesaramilli village of Gudlavalleu mandal, was the founder of ([[Andhra Patrika]], first telugu newspaper and also company which manufactures ayurvedic pain balm called Amrutanjan.
* [[Pingali Venkayya]] was born in Bhatlapenumarru, near Machilipatnam, was a freedom fighter and was known as designer of [[Indian National Flag]].
* [[C. K. Nayudu|Cottari Kanakaiya Nayudu]] was born in Machilipatnam. He served as the first-ever captain of the Indian national cricket team.
* [[N. T. Rama Rao]] popularly referred to by his initials NTR, was an Indian actor, filmmaker and a Chief Minister of Andhra Pradesh. He was born in Nimmakuru of Gudivada mandal.
* [[Narla Venkateswara Rao]] was a Telugu language writer, journalist and politician from Andhra Pradesh in India. He was Rajya Sabha member twice from 3 April 1958 to 2 April 1970, and wrote a satakam in Telugu along with several other books.
* [[Narla Tata Rao]] was a prominent person in the power sector of India and a former chairman of the Andhra Pradesh State Electricity Board. He was born in [[Kavutaram]]
* [[Patcha Ramachandra Rao]] was a distinguished metallurgist and administrator. He was born in Kavutaram in Krishna District
* [[Kaikala Satyanarayana]] was an Indian actor, producer, director, and politician who predominantly worked in Telugu cinema. He was born in Kavutaram village in Krishna district.

